    "explanation": "To both parties: the rider's route-deviation complaint is made out on the merits, but the AI cannot issue the refund this dispute warrants, so the case goes to a human reviewer and the 6.50 SGD contested is held, neither collected nor refunded. Here is why, limb by limb. (1) The deviation: POL-RD-22 takes it from the platform's own recorded distances — 24.8 km driven against 20.5 km on the recommended route (EV-TRIP-00902, weight 1.0) — which is 4.30 km, over four times the 1.0 km tolerance; the sparse GPS trace (EV-GPS-00902) is not used to re-measure distance, as POL-RD-22 itself says. (2) Traffic justification: the reroute was justified under POL-RD-23 by the two PIE advisories — EV-ADVIS-00902-01 (HIGH-severity vehicle fire, an 'incident' type) and EV-ADVIS-00902-02 (HEAVY_CONGESTION at the airport exit) — each of which intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window; EV-ADVIS-00902-03 (ECP, TRAFFIC_FLOW, no intersection) justifies nothing and is neutral. (3) Notification: the driver did not inform the rider of the deviation as POL-RD-21 requires — the chat log (EV-CHAT-00902, weight 1.0) shows the rider raising the route herself at 13:24 and the driver replying only that he knew the way — so the deviation was not agreed. (4) On those facts POL-RD-24 row (b) applies (traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km), and the excess distance fare is 4.30 km x 0.80 SGD per km = 3.44 SGD, per POL-RD-24 and its no-surge threshold; the 6.50 SGD asked (the 35.00 charged less the 28.50 quote) is not a measure the policy provides, so the balance of that claim fails. (5) The obstacle is confidence. The 0.80 per-km rate is carried only by the fare breakdown, EV-FARE-00902, which is impaired at weight 0.75 (PARTIAL_RECORD — the ledger exported no line items). Under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence is capped at that 0.75, and POL-RD-25 permits an AI ruling on a route deviation only at a confidence of 0.80 or more. The 6.50 SGD value is